<title>USA: Nationwide farm revenue insurance proposed in FY98.</title>
<headline>Nationwide farm revenue insurance proposed in FY98.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The White House, as part of its fiscal 1998 budget proposal, asked Thursday for nationwide availability of revenue insurance for farmers.</p>
<p>The insurance gives farmers protection against low prices and poor yields. It was offered on a trial basis in 1996 in a few states.</p>
<p>Federal Crop Insurance Corp announced last week that three versions of the coverage would be offered in a wider area this year.</p>
<p>&quot;Legislation...would allow the corporaton to offer revenue insurance products on a nationwide basis,&quot; budget documents stated.</p>
<p>The administration also said it would adjust FCIC loss ratios &quot;to a more actuarially sound level.&quot;</p>
</text>
